  "category" : "Mental Health",
  "createdAt" : 1746221756,
  "description" : "<b>Data source description</b>: BRFSS measures health-related risk behaviors, chronic health conditions, and use of preventive services among U.S. adults through telephone interviews. BRFSS collects data in all 50 states as well as the District of Columbia and three U.S. territories of Guam, Puerto Rico, and U.S. Virgin Islands. Responses were used to produce estimates of experiences, behaviors, and conditions related to mental health and well-being for participating jurisdictions. Nationwide estimates are not available.  \n\n \n\n<b>For additional information, please see</b>: <a href = \"https://www.cdc.gov/mental-health/about-data/mental-health-data-sources.html\" target =\"_blank\">Mental Health Data Sources</a>.",
